# Hand-authored frond stamps: one folder per source, each holding a diffuse
# (sRGB, alpha carries the cutout) and, optionally, an arm and a 16-bit disp
# map — either one absent is derived from the diffuse. One whole frond per
# stamp, base on the bottom edge and tip at the top, standing the way it is
# drawn — like a clump stamp, nothing here is ever rotated. `source.json`
# declares lengthMetres. No normal map — scatter-forge derives it from the
# height. See ../../../../docs/scatter-forge/authored-art.md.
#
# Large binaries, kept out of git the way /assets/ is. With no source here the
# forge generates its fronds instead, so a fresh clone still builds. This rule
# keeps the file itself tracked so the folder survives that clone.
*
!.gitignore
